-- Tier 1 and tier 2 tests.
--
-- Tier 1 is the test table on the left of Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov
-- & Gelbard (2025), the SimpLEX screen capture, transcribed row for row and
-- run against the text it was written for: the draft. The draft is reached by
-- name, never by date, because it was never in force and has no commencement
-- to pin -- see the long comment in hvac-fees.l4.
--
-- Tier 2 runs the SAME four scenarios against the law as it actually stood, at
-- three dates on L4's rule-effective-time axis: before the Regulations
-- commenced, under the text as made (16 July 2025), and under the text as
-- amended (4 May 2026). There is only ONE rule for regulation 2 now; every
-- difference below comes from the date the axis is pinned to, not from a
-- different rule. Every assertion here is satisfied; the point is that the
-- answers move. The companion file hvac-tests-simplex-red.l4 runs the draft's
-- EXPECTATIONS against the Regulations as made and is meant to fail, and
-- check.sh counts its failures.
@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-fees`

§ `Three days to ask the same question on`

-- Shorthands for the three vintages, so that every tier 2 line below reads as
-- a date and not as a magic number. `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` takes a
-- DATE; these ARE the vintages, and they are dates rather than enum tags
-- precisely because each one is a day on which the instrument really stood in
-- a particular form.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `a day before the Regulations commenced` @nlg a day before the Fees Regulations commenced
                                               @nlg:he יום שלפני תחילתן של תקנות האגרות
    IS YMD 2025 7 1

GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `a day under the Regulations as made` @nlg a day on which the Fees Regulations stood as made
                                            @nlg:he יום שבו עמדו תקנות האגרות כנוסחן עם התקנתן
    IS `the day the Regulations came into force`

GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `a day under the Regulations as amended` @nlg a day on which the Fees Regulations stood as amended
                                               @nlg:he יום שבו עמדו תקנות האגרות כנוסחן לאחר תיקון התשפ"ו
    IS `the day the 5786 amendment came into force`

§ `Tier 1 -- the SimpLEX test table, in its own words`

-- SimpLEX's table has three columns: scenario, expected outcome, citation. Its
-- outcomes are the three phrases below, not TRUE and FALSE, so the rows are
-- asserted here in exactly those words. (The screenshot's second table, "test
-- scenarios for fee updates and the index", shows only its heading and its
-- citations -- Law s.59, regs 2(a)-(c) -- so its rows cannot be transcribed.)
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `registration approved`     -- הרשמה מאושרת
    `appeal under review`       -- הערעור נבדק
    `registration refused`      -- הרשמה נדחית

-- The table, run against the draft. No date: a draft has none.
GIVEN service IS A Service
      paid    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Outcome
DECIDE `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` @nlg what SimpLEX's table would show for %service% under the draft when %paid% shekels have been paid
                                                     @nlg:he מה שטבלת SimpLEX הייתה מציגה בעד %service% לפי הטיוטה כאשר שולמו %paid% שקלים
    IS IF NOT `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` service paid
       THEN `registration refused`
       ELSE CONSIDER service
            WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN `appeal under review`
            WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN `appeal under review`
            OTHERWISE `registration approved`

-- The same table, run against the law as it actually stood on the rule-effective
-- date. One rule; the vintage comes from the axis.
GIVEN service IS A Service
      paid    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Outcome
DECIDE `the SimpLEX outcome for` @nlg what SimpLEX's table would show for %service% when %paid% shekels have been paid, under the Fees Regulations as they stood on the rule-effective date
                                @nlg:he מה שטבלת SimpLEX הייתה מציגה בעד %service% כאשר שולמו %paid% שקלים, לפי תקנות האגרות כנוסחן ביום החל על הדין
    IS IF NOT `the service may be provided` service paid
       THEN `registration refused`
       ELSE CONSIDER service
            WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN `appeal under review`
            WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN `appeal under review`
            OTHERWISE `registration approved`

-- #  scenario                                            expected outcome           citation
-- 5  registration for a theoretical examination          registration approved      reg. 2(a)
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `theoretical examination` 273 EQUALS `registration approved`
-- 6  registration for a practical examination            registration approved      reg. 2(b)
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `practical examination` 194 EQUALS `registration approved`
-- 7  appeal with payment (40 NIS)                        appeal under review        reg. 2(c)
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40 EQUALS `appeal under review`
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40 EQUALS `appeal under review`
-- 8  registration for an examination without payment    registration refused       reg. 4
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `theoretical examination` 0 EQUALS `registration refused`
#ASSERT `the outcome the SimpLEX draft would show for` `practical examination` 0 EQUALS `registration refused`

-- The same four rows, as the Regulations as made would have shown them:
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the SimpLEX outcome for` `theoretical examination` 273)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the SimpLEX outcome for` `theoretical examination` 0)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the SimpLEX outcome for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the SimpLEX outcome for` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40)

§ `Tier 1 -- the SimpLEX test table, against the draft it was written for`

-- Fig. 4, "test scenarios for professional examinations", relevant provisions
-- "Law -- s.9 | Regulations -- 2(a)-(h)":
--   #5  registration for a theoretical examination  -> registration approved   (reg. 2(a))
--   #6  registration for a practical examination    -> registration approved   (reg. 2(b))
--   #7  appeal with payment (40 NIS)                -> appeal under review      (reg. 2(c))
--   #8  registration for an examination, no payment -> registration refused    (reg. 4)
-- and the worked example beneath the table: "the candidate registered for a
-- theoretical examination but did not pay the fee ... outcome: registration
-- refused -- a duty to pay the fee".

#ASSERT `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `theoretical examination` EQUALS JUST 273
#ASSERT `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `practical examination`   EQUALS JUST 194

-- #5
#ASSERT     `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `theoretical examination` 273
-- #6
#ASSERT     `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `practical examination` 194
-- #7, both halves of "theoretical or practical"
#ASSERT     `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40
#ASSERT     `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40
-- #8, and the worked example
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `theoretical examination` 0
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `practical examination` 0
-- underpayment is not payment "in full" (reg. 4)
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` `theoretical examination` 272
-- The draft's own aggregate: 2(c) adds the 40 to "the fee under (a)", the
-- theoretical fee, whichever examination is appealed -- so 313 either way (F5).
#ASSERT `the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for` `appeal against a practical examination score`   EQUALS JUST 313
#ASSERT `the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` EQUALS JUST 313
-- The draft prices the APPLICATION for a licence, not its receipt (F5).
#ASSERT `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `application for a licence`       EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `receipt or renewal of a licence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The draft's foreign-expert fee, cited to "s. 8 of the Law" [sic -- s.9 in the
-- bill and in the Act; the wrong cross-reference is preserved deliberately].
#ASSERT `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `temporary licence for a foreign expert` EQUALS JUST 398

§ `Tier 2 -- before the Regulations commenced`

-- Asking the same rule about a day before 16 July 2025 is not a trick question
-- and does not answer 0. Nothing is prescribed, because no such rule was yet in
-- force -- and reg. 4 therefore has nothing to withhold, so every service is
-- allowed on a payment of nothing.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`)                     EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`)                   EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the fee prescribed for` `receipt or renewal of a licence`)           EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the fee prescribed for` `temporary licence for a foreign expert`)    EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the service may be provided` `practical examination` 0)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day before the Regulations commenced` (`the SimpLEX outcome for` `practical examination` 0) EQUALS `registration approved`
-- The day before commencement is still "before": the boundary is inclusive at
-- 16 July, not at 15 July.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 15) (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 16) (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`) EQUALS JUST 194

§ `Tier 2 -- the same scenarios against the Regulations as made`

-- The theoretical examination had NO fee in the Regulations as made, so
-- reg. 4 has nothing to withhold: scenario #8's candidate, who did not pay,
-- is admitted to the theoretical examination.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 0)
-- The practical examination and its fee survived unchanged.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`) EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `practical examination` 194)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `practical examination` 0)
-- The appeal fee attaches to "the examination score", and the only examination
-- the text as made knows is the practical one (reg. 1, and (b)'s own pointer to (a)).
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `appeal against a practical examination score` 0)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the service may be provided` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 0)
-- What an appellant tenders in all, as made: 2(b) points at (a), the practical fee.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   EQUALS JUST 234
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The licence fee MOVED from the application to the receipt (fork F5): the
-- draft's 2(d) charged "בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון", the text as made charges
-- "בעד קבלת רישיון". Under the draft a refused applicant has paid 284; as
-- made nothing falls due until the licence issues.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `application for a licence`)       EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `receipt or renewal of a licence`) EQUALS JUST 284
-- The foreign-expert fee is as drafted.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made` (`the fee prescribed for` `temporary licence for a foreign expert`) EQUALS JUST 398

§ `Tier 2 -- the same scenarios against the Regulations as amended`

-- The 5786 amendment put the theoretical examination fee back, at 158 rather
-- than the draft's 273, so scenario #8 refuses again -- and #5's candidate,
-- who paid the draft's 273, has overpaid.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 0)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 158)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 273)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 157)
-- The appeal fee MOVED: as amended it attaches to the theoretical score and no
-- longer to the practical one.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `appeal against a practical examination score` 0)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the service may be provided` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 0)
-- What an appellant tenders in all, as amended: 2(b) points at (a1), the theoretical fee.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) EQUALS JUST 198
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   EQUALS NOTHING
-- Nothing else moved between as-made and as-amended.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`)                  EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `receipt or renewal of a licence`)        EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `temporary licence for a foreign expert`) EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `application for a licence`)              EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tier 2 -- the day the amendment commenced`

-- The amending regulations, KT 12383 of 4 May 2026, state no commencement, so
-- they commenced on publication (Interpretation Ordinance [New Version] s.17;
-- see hvac-fees.l4 and fork F6). The boundary is therefore 4 May, not 11 May --
-- and the assertions below are what would go red if fork F6 were resolved the
-- other way.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 3)  (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 4)  (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 11) (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 3)  (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 4)  (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tier 2 -- what the texts say, side by side`

-- The draft, off the axis, and the two enacted vintages on it.
#EVAL `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `theoretical examination`
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made`    (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`)
#EVAL `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `appeal against a practical examination score`
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made`    (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as made`    (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `a day under the Regulations as amended` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`)
